WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:05.381
Whether or not you enjoy Big Brother, Survivor,
or Keeping Up With the Kardashians, there's

00:00:05.381 --> 00:00:09.520
no denying that these long-running reality
shows have figured out a winning formula.

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:11.520
But a lot of shows weren't so lucky.

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:15.640
Things can go wrong on set all the time, and
when dealing with regular amateurs instead

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:19.860
of professional actors or experienced showbiz
vets, that risk is even greater.

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:24.720
From hardcore drug use to gruesome felonies,
these reality series all got canceled due

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:26.280
to some major mistakes.

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:27.640
Pretty stupid

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:33.240
It isn't easy keeping up with the Kardashians,
which Alexis Neiers and her family found out

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:37.450
the hard way while making their E! reality
series Pretty Wild, which ran for only one

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:39.080
season in 2010.

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:43.900
The show followed Alexis, her sisters, and
their mom, former Playmate Andrea Arlington.

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:48.660
Alexis was arrested for participating in the
infamous Hollywood "Bling Ring," and jailed

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:51.980
for robbing Orlando Bloom's house, all in
the first episode!

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:56.140
While the legal trouble so early on should
have been something of a red flag, the clincher

00:00:56.140 --> 00:01:00.520
came later when photos were leaked of Alexis
and her sister Tess smoking.

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:03.500
The show was canceled for good, and both girls
attended rehab.

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:08.120
"December 1st, 2010 was the last time I used."

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:10.120
Armed and foolish

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:14.980
You'd think the only idiot mistake in a show
called Armed and Famous would be the premise:

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:19.090
training celebrities to be police officers,
and actually making them do the job while

00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:20.740
being filmed for a TV show.

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:22.740
"No John is going to hurt these two girls.

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:23.620
Not on my watch!"

00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:25.820
The stupid doesn't stop there, though.

00:01:25.829 --> 00:01:31.189
The 2007 reality TV dud was canceled after
just four episodes when a woman filed a lawsuit

00:01:31.189 --> 00:01:33.860
against CBS Broadcasting for $1 million.

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:37.960
Apparently the famous cops had ransacked her
apartment looking for two suspects before

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:40.180
realizing they were at the wrong address.

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:44.540
The network also cited the show's low ratings
as part of the reason for the cancellation.

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:46.160
Editing error

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:50.619
There's nothing quite like stripping contestants
of all their clothing to raise the stakes

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:51.620
on a reality series.

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:55.140
This was the simple concept behind VH1's Dating.

00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:59.300
Contestants disrobed down to their birthday
suits and went on "dates" such as sipping

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:03.170
cocktails by the pool or engaging in some
light mud wrestling.

00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:03.980
Romantic, right?

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:08.000
Although the participants needed to bare it
all during filming, they were apparently promised

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:10.440
that their naughty bits would be blurred out
when the show aired.

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:15.100
Unfortunately, whoever was in charge of the
blurring made a major error during the July

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:17.120
31st, 2014 broadcast.

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:21.170
Then-28-year-old model Jessie Nizewitz was
wrestling with her date on the beach when

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:24.260
viewers caught a brief unblurred glimpse of
her private parts.

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:28.620
Nizewitz quickly became the target of ridicule
across social media, and filed an ultimately

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:33.540
unsuccessful $10 million lawsuit against VH1
owner Viacom, along with two of the show's

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:34.560
production companies.

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:38.780
Eventually the Parents' Television Council,
who were staunchly against the show, managed

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:42.700
to wrestle 90 percent of Dating corporate
advertisers away from the series.

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:47.700
The show was canceled shortly after its third
season in 2017, with poor ratings cited as

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.500
one of several reasons for the decision.

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:51.180
Good grief

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:56.290
If you thought the world of funeral homes
was an untapped treasure trove of reality

00:02:56.290 --> 00:02:58.320
gold, well, there might be a reason for that.

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:03.320
In 2014, Lifetime was set to produce Good
Grief, a reality series that centered around

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:06.100
the Johnson Family Mortuary in Fort Worth,
Texas.

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:09.420
But the series wound up six feet under before
it ever got off the ground.

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:14.550
On July 15th, 2014, the landlord paid his
tenants a visit and discovered eight rotting

00:03:14.550 --> 00:03:16.460
bodies hidden beneath the funeral home.

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:21.520
When reporters and paparazzi showed up, owner
Dondre Johnson initially told the spectators,

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:25.560
"That's great advertising, because in a few
days from now we'll be on a reality show so

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:26.760
I want all this media."

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:30.920
Ultimately, Johnson was found guilty of theft
for stealing money from customers and neglecting

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:35.670
the bodies of their loved ones, and sentenced
to two years in prison and a fine of $10,000.

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:37.860
Unsurprisingly, the network pulled the plug.

